# Testing Rules

- JUnit 5 + Mockito (BDDMockito style) + Testcontainers for integration tests.
- Three test types — use the right slice for each:
  - Service logic → `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` — no Spring context
  - Controller → `@WebMvcTest({Controller}.class)` — web layer only
  - Repository queries → `@DataJpaTest` + Testcontainers PostgreSQL — never H2
- Test class naming: `{ClassName}Test` — same package as the class under test.
- Test method naming states behaviour: `methodName_scenario_expectedBehaviour`
  - e.g. `create_whenDuplicateEmail_throwsConflictException`
- Each test independent and runnable in any order — no shared mutable state between tests.
- BDDMockito style only: `given(...).willReturn(...)` / `then(...).should(...)` — never `when()` / `verify()`.
- AssertJ `assertThat()` for all assertions — never JUnit `assertEquals()` or `assertTrue()`.
- Always test: happy path + `ResourceNotFoundException` + `ValidationException` at minimum.
- Coverage minimum 80% instruction coverage — measured and enforced via JaCoCo `jacoco:check`.
- Use real PostgreSQL via Testcontainers — never H2 in-memory (different SQL dialect, no constraints).
- `@DynamicPropertySource` to inject Testcontainers connection properties.
- Inject `Clock` for time-dependent code — never call `LocalDateTime.now()` directly in business logic.
- `@WebMvcTest` controller tests always include a `400` test with invalid/missing required field.
- `@WebMvcTest` controller tests always include a `401` test verifying unauthenticated access is blocked.
- `StepVerifier` for reactive (WebFlux) service tests — never `.block()` in tests except as last resort.

